      "worked_solution": "We count the number of pentagons. We see that there are $2$ pentagons.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $4$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is $2:4.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to the total shapes is $1:2.$",
